repository-code: "https://github.com/tranducle/RAISR-SME"
url: "https://raisr-sme.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the RAISR-SME v1.0 25-item ternary cyber-AI
  self-assessment checklist and deterministic empirical/simulation audit suite
  for ICIIT 2027. Includes the frozen item bank (bank_v1.json), authoritative
  NIST CSF 2.0 subcategory crosswalk and verifier (verify_ids.py), three
  bit-exact scoring engines (Python stdlib, browser JavaScript, and NumPy),
  automated parity tests across 20,006 vectors, retrospective completion-bound
  and boundary-sensitivity audits (retrospective_robustness.py), and four
  analysis suites (exp1 to exp4) auditing UK Cyber Security Breaches Survey
  (2023 to 2025) skip-routing and size strata, UK Cyber Security Longitudinal
  Survey (Waves 1 to 4) matched-panel timing and Mundlak models, and 50,000
  synthetic SME profiles. Licensed UK Data Archive microdata is withheld per
  End User Licence and documented with SHA-256 checksums in DATA.md and
  data/README.md.
keywords:
  - SME cybersecurity
  - responsible AI
  - formative scoring
  - unknown responses
  - survey measurement
  - synthetic evaluation
license: MIT
version: "2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
